# Copy this file to `dev.env` and put your key in it, then reload the extension.
#
#   cp dev.env.example dev.env
#
# background.js reads dev.env at startup and seeds the key into chrome.storage
# if none is saved yet, so a fresh browser profile does not mean pasting it into
# the popup again.
#
# dev.env is gitignored, and package-extension.sh refuses to build if it is
# present in the staged output, so a key cannot reach the Chrome Web Store this
# way. It is still a plaintext key on disk in a directory Chrome loads: fine on
# a machine you control, wrong on a shared one.
#
# The key is seeded UNVERIFIED. The popup will say "saved but never verified"
# until you re-save it there, which checks it against the API.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here
